1G         [81G            [94G      [101G      [108G  │[112G     [118G      [125G    [130G    [135G   [139G         [149G        [158G          [169G [171G     After     [187G        [196G           [208G          [219G         [229G        [238G         │[K[2C[1B├────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤[2C[1B│[13Gal │ [38;2;177;185;249mpersistent.kind[39m is f[40Ge text defaulting to [38;2;177;185;249m'fact'[39m; 147 of 157 rows are [38;2;177;185;249mfact[39m         [103G       │ Kind constrained to[132GLayer-1 classes; fine type[159Gin [38;2;177;185;249montology_class[39m     [182G            [195G               [247G│[2C[1B├────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤[2C[1B│ Graph      │ 23 entities, 0 grounded; [38;2;177;185;249mancestors()[39m never[61Gr[64Gurns anything, so[82Gsubclass expansion is inert │ [38;2;177;185;249mmetadata.ontology_ancestors[39m populates, and [38;2;177;185;249mexpand()[39m's shared-entity join reach[191Gs [194G claim about [38;2;177;185;249mpgv[211Gctor[39m from a qu[226Gry about [38;2;177;185;249mVectorStore[39m │[249G[K[2C[1B├────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤[2C[1B│[5GVector[16G│[18G[38;2;177;185;249mentities.embedding[37G[39mis[40Gdeclared[49Gand[53G[1mnever written[110G[22m│[112GGrounding[122Gproduces[131Ga[133Gcanonical[143Gname[148Gworth[154Gembedding[164G—[166Galias[172Gcollapse[181Gcuts[186Gsynonym[194Gfragmentation[208G[3mbefore[215G[23mthe[219Gvector[226Gis[229Gcomputed[247G│[2C[1B└────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘[2C[2BOne gap outranks the ontology for your stated goal of decision support: [38;2;177;185;249mchose[39m and [38;2;177;185;249mover[39m edges point at [1mliteral strings[22m, not entities ([38;2;177;185;249mcompile.py:518-524[39m), and the [38;2;177;185;249mdecisions[39m/[38;2;177;185;249mrewards[39m ledger has no edge into [38;2;177;185;249mpersistent[39m at all. Eight decision claims exist[2C[1Band[7Gnon[11G of[15Gthem[20Gcan[24Gbe[27Gaggregated[38Gor[41Gscored[48Gagainst[56Goutcome. Grounding[75Gthe[79Galternatives[92Gas[95Gentities[104Gis[107Gwhat[112Gturns[118G"what[124Gdid[128GI[130Gdecide"[138Ginto[143G"what[149Gdid[153GI[155Gdecide[162Gabout[168GX,[171Gand[175Gdid it[182Gwork."[247G[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mD. First question[22m[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1BEve[7Gyt[10Ging[14Gabove holds under one assumption I should confi[62Gm rather than [77Gue[80Gs: how many scopes th[104Ghas [109Go serve. If [38;2;177;185;249mharness[39m is the only rea[145G group, Layer 2 and the T-Box scope f[183Glter ar[191G spe[196Gulative and I'd cut[216Gthe[221Gtoday. If [38;2;177;185;249mcareer-ops[39m and[K[2C[1B[38;2;177;185;249mTrading-Bot[39m are joining, the filter is a prerequisite, not a nice-to-have.[K[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m● [39mUser answered Claude's questions:[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Which project groups is this ontology actually going to serve? Right now the DB has exactly one real scope — `harness` (arteries, capillaries, marrow) — plus 270 junk /tmp rows. `heart` and `plexus` exist on disk but aren't tracked. → Harness + [2C[1B[39m   [38;2;153;153;153mmany, growing over time[39m[K[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39m[1mSettled:[12G[22mLayer[18G2[20Gand[24Gthe[28GT-Box[34Gscope[40Gfilter[47Gare[51Gprerequisites,[66Gnot[70Gextension[80Gpoints[87G—[89GI'll[94Gtreat[100G[38;2;177;185;249montology_bindings[118G[39m+[120Ga[122Gscope-filtered[137G[38;2;177;185;249m_lookup()[147G[39mas[150Gblocking[159Gwork[164Gbefore[171Gany[175Gdomain[182Gvocabulary[193Ggets[198Gloaded.[206GIt[209Galso[214Gmeans[220Gthe[224Gvocabulary[235Gauthorship[246Gloop[251Gand[2C[1Ba growth budget are[23Gpart[28Gof[31Gthe[35Gdesign,[43Gnot[47Gan[50Gafterthought.[2C[2B[1mOpened:[22m at[14G~20 tracked[26Grepos, scope [3mgranularity[23m stops being cosmetic. E[75Gtitie[81G are unique per [38;2;177;185;249m(scope_id, kind, lower(name))[39m, so the number of scopes is exactly the number of times a shared[192Gnoun [198Gike [38;2;177;185;249mpgvector[39m or [38;2;177;185;249mPostgres[39m gets[228Gduplicated as[244G unrelated[2C[1Bnode — and duplicated nodes can'[36G produce the shared-enti[61Gy trav[68Grsal that[78G[38;2;177;185;249mexpand()[87G[39mdepends[95Gon[98G(your[104Glive[109Ggraph:[116G68[119G[38;2;177;185;249mmentions[128G[39medges[134Gdoing[140Gthe[144Gheavy[150Glifting[158Gagainst[166G33[169Gdirect[176Gclaim-to-claim[191Gedges).[7C[3B[38;2;153;153;153mAt ~20 tracked [24Gepo[28G, how should scopes be cut? This[61Gdecides the en[76Gity nam[84Gspace —[92Gand it's the [106Gxpensiv[115Gone to change later, since reg[146Gouping means[159Gre-keying entity nodes and[186Gre-derivi[196Gg[198Gtheir edg[208Gs. →[213GScope[219G should follow whatever[243Ggroup I[251G[39m[K[5C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mdefine. Some repos[25Gare their own scopes (only one repo in group) while others like harness contain multiple repos (capillaries, arteries, heart, plexus, marrow noting I haven't done more work on heart, plexus and marrow yet) [11C[2B[39mscope[18Gmembers[26Gip stays hand-defined — which is alr[63Gady exactly what[80G[38;2;177;185;249mart scope add[94G[39mdo[97Gs,[100Gso no mechanism change[123G. Card[130Gnality[137Gis arbitrary: m[153Gstly singletons, [38;2;177;185;249mharness[39m [179Gs the one clust[195Gr (and it should get [38;2;177;185;249mheart[39m and [38;2;177;185;249mplexus[39m added now, even[K[2C[1Bunworked, so thei[21G firs[28Gcommit[35Glands in the righ[53G namespace[64Grather[71Gthan[76Gminting[84Ga[86Gscope-of-one).[2C[2B[1mCons[8Gquence to park:[22m with mostly-singleton scope[52G, a cross-cutting noun l[77Gke [38;2;177;185;249mpgvector[39m or [38;2;177;185;249mPostgres[39m becomes ~15 unrelated nodes. Whether that's[145Ga problem[155Gdepends[163Gentirely on the n[181Gxt answer,[192Gs[194G I'm not designing around it[223Gy[226G.[228G[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[1B[48;2;177;185;249m[38;2;0;0;0m ☐ Target query [1B[39m[49m[K[1B[2m│[22m [38;2;255;255;255m[1mSix months from now, what is the ONE question you most want to type and get a real answer to? Ontology is driven by query — this decides which relations get built and which linkage work is worth doing.[22m[39m[K[5C[1B[K[1B[38;2;177;185;249m❯[3G[38;2;153;153;153m1.[6G[38;2;177;185;249m"What did I decide here, and why?"[1B[39m [3G   [38;2;153;153;153mDecision recall inside one project. Needs `chose`/`over` pointing at entities instead of literal strings (compile.py:518), and rationale surfaced with the decision. Cheapest to build — 8 decision claims already exist, just unusable.[239G[39m[K[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153m2.[39m "What have I learned ab[30Gut X[35Ganywhere?"[K[5C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mCross-project technical transfer — a Postgres lesson from arteries reaching Trading-Bot. Forces the shared tech entity layer and a cross-scope read path that does not exist today (SCOPE_CTE stops at the group).[2C[1B3.[39m "Which of my decisions[29Gactually worked?"[K[5C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mOutcome-linked recall. Needs the `decisions`/`rewards` ledger edged into `persistent` — they are completely disconnected today — plus a way to close the loop on a decision months later.[1B[39m [3G[38;2;153;153;153m4.[39m "What is true right now vs. what changed?"[1B     [7G[38;2;153;153;153memporal[15Gstat[20G.[22GNeeds [29Geal validity semantic[51G: `invalidated_by` with a reason, `measured_at` for numbers, and a rule for when a superseded fact stays readable. You tombstone with valid_until but never record why.[2C[1B5. Type something.[1B──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[1B[39m  6.[6GChat[11Gabout[17Gthis[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153mEnter to select ·[19G↑/↓ to n[28Gvigate · Esc to [45Gancel[39m[K[59;1H[47;1H[?2026l(B[?1000h[?1002h[?1003h[?1006h(B[?1000h[?1002h[?1003h[?1006h(B[?1000h[?1002h[?1003h[?1006h(B[?1000h[?1002h[?1003h[?1006h(B[?1000h[?1002h[?1003h[?1006h[?2026h[H[46B [6G"What did I decide here, and why?"[2B[38;2;177;185;249m❯[6G"What have I learned about X anywhere?"[39m[59;1H[49;1H[?2026l[?2026h[H[48B [6G"What have I learned about X anywhere?"[2B[38;2;177;185;249m❯[6G"Which of my decisions actually worked?"[39m[59;1H[51;1H[?2026l[?2026h[H[50B [6G"Which of my decisions actually worked?"[2B[38;2;177;185;249m❯[6G"What is true 