ith building out [1B[39m     [38;2;153;153;153mprojects in noncontradictory ways (ex. building feature A at first with details 1, 2, 3 but wanting to build feature B later with details 4, 5 conflicting with 1, 2 meaning I need help resolving these issues) but I'd like all 4 eventually[1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39m[1mSettled, and it sharpens the whole design.[22m You don't want decision [3mrecall[23m — you want [1mconflict detection at design time[22m: when you spec feature B, the graph must surface the prior decisions and constraints that details 4 and 5 violate.[2B [3GThat changes what the ontolog[33G has to make work. Cosine[59Gsimilarity won't find these — "featur[97G A[100Gkeys memories by UUID" and "feature B keys by repo[151Gpath" are semantically dist[179Gnt but structurally in[202Gconflict.[212GWhat finds them is the [1mshared-entity arm of[2C[1B[38;2;177;185;249mexpand()[22m[39m ([38;2;177;185;249mgraph.py:110[39m),[28Gwhere both claims reach [53Ghe same entity node. Which [81Gs precisely why grounding[107Gis[110Gload-bearing:[124Gif[127Gone[131Gclaim[137Gsays[142G[38;2;177;185;249mprimary key[154G[39mand[158Gthe[162Gother[168Gsays[173G[38;2;177;185;249mid column[39m,[184Gthey[189Ghave[194Gto[197Gcollapse[206Gto[209Gone[213Gnode[218Gor[221Gthe[225Gconflict[234Gis[237Ginvisible.[248GYour[2C[1B0/23[8Ggrounding[18Grate[23Gis[26Gthe[30Greason[37Gthis[42Gdoesn't[50Gwork[55Gtoday.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BIt[6Galso[11Gpromotes[20G[38;2;177;185;249mconstraint[31G[39mfrom[36Ga[38Gfootnote[47Gto[50Ga[52Gfirst-class[64Gclaim[70Gkind[75G—[77Gand[81Gthere[87Gis[90Gexactly[98G[1m1 constraint[111G[22min[114Gthe[118Gdatabase,[128Gagainst[136G147[140Gfacts.[1B[38;2;153;153;153m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[1B←[3G[48;2;177;185;249m[38;2;0;0;0m ☐ Capture path [39m[49m ✔ Submit  →[K[5C[1B[K[1B[2m│[3G[22m[38;2;255;255;255m[1mWhere should design constraints and decisions actually come from? Conflict detection is only as good as its input, and right now the store holds 147 facts, 8 decisions, and 1 constraint — mostly narration of work already done.[1B[22m[39m[K[1B[38;2;177;185;249m❯[3G[38;2;153;153;153m1.[6G[39m[[8G][10G[38;2;177;185;249mTune the compiler to hunt them[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mRewrite COMPILE_SYSTEM to actively extract constraints and decisions with their rationale, instead of treating them as one kind among four. Zero workflow change for you, but the compiler is already the source of the narration problem.[39m[K[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153m2.[39m [ ] Explicit capture at decide-time[K[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mAn `art decide` / `art constrain` command you run when you actually make the call. Highest precision, survives `ARTERIES_EPHEMERAL=keep`, but only works if you remember to type it.[2C[1B3.[6G[39m[[8G][10GIngest[17Gdesign[24Gdocs[29Gand[33GADRs[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153m`art docs` already writes reviewed claims with path/line/digest provenance. Plans and specs in the repo become constraints. Good fit if your design intent lives in files — useless if it lives only in conversation.[2C[1B4.[6G[39m[[8G][10GFrom[15Gplexus/heart[28Gas[31Gthey[36Gdecompose[46Ggoals[1B [3G[38;2;153;153;153mThe orchestration layer records d[37Gcisions as structured events while running. Most automatic and most durable, but depends on plexus and heart, which you said you haven't worked on yet.[1B[39m  [38;2;153;153;153m5. [39m[ ] [38;2;153;153;153mType[15Gsomething[39m[K[5C[1B[1mSubmit[1B[22m[38;2;153;153;153m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────