 real answer to? Ontology is driven by query — this decides which relations get built and which linkage work is worth doing. → 1 because that helps with building out [5C[1Bprojects in noncontradictory ways (ex. building feature A at first with details 1, 2, 3 but wanting to build feature B later with details 4, 5 conflicting with 1, 2 meaning I need help resolving these issues) but I'd like all 4 eventually[1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[39m [1mSettled, and it sharpens the whole design.[22m You don't want decision [3mrecall[23m — you want [1mconflict detection at design time[22m: when you spec feature B, the graph must surface the prior decisions and constraints that details 4 and 5 violate.[K[5C[1B[K[2C[1BThat[8Gchanges[16Gwhat[21Gthe[25Gontology[34Ghas[38Gto[41Gmake[46Gwork.[52GCosine[59Gsimilarity[70Gwon't[76Gfind[81Gthese[87G—[89G"feature[98GA[100Gkeys[105Gmemories[114Gby[117GUUID"[123Gand[127G"feature[136GB[138Gkeys[143Gby[146Grepo[151Gpath"[157Gare[161Gsemantically[174Gdistant[182Gbut[186Gstructurally[199Gin[202Gconflict.[212GWhat[217Gfinds[223Gthem[228Gis[231Gthe[235G[1mshared-entity arm of[1B[22m [3G[38;2;177;185;249m[1mexpand()[12G[22m[39m([38;2;177;185;249mgraph.py:110[39m), where both claims reach the[56Gsame entity node. Which[80Gis precisely why grounding is load-bearing: if one c[133Gaim[137Gsays [38;2;177;185;249mprimary key[39m and[158Gthe other says [38;2;177;185;249mid column[39m, they[189Ghave to[197Gcollapse t[208G one node or the conflict is invisible. Your[2C[1B0/23 grounding rate [24Gs [27Ghe reason this doesn't work today.[K[2C[2BIt also promotes [38;2;177;185;249mconstraint[39m from a footn[44Gte t[49G a first-class claim[70Gkind[75G— and there is exactly [1m1 constraint[22m in th[117G database, against 147 facts.[147G[K[7C[3B[38;2;153;153;153mWhere should design cons[33Grain[38Gs and deci[49Gions[54Gactually[63Gcome[68Gfrom? Conflict detection is only as g[106God as its [117Gnput, and [128Gight now[137Gthe store holds 147 facts, 8 decisions, and[181G1 constraint[194G— mostly[203Gnarration of work already done. → From plexus/heart [5C[1Bas they decompose go[27Gls, "On[35Gtop of initia[49G spec impo[60Gts from plexus/heart [82Gnd docs, things[98GI pla[104G out[109Gshould also be taken into account.[144GWhen[157Gs arise,[166Gmy[169Ggoal is to be able to[191Gs[193Ge them along w[208Gth retrieved context for evidence, then I'll [5C[1Bdecide what design/feature to actually follow while you work on resolving implementation details to satisfy that"[1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39m[1mSettled — and this is the operating loop, stated cleanly:[2C[1B[22m[K[2C[1B[2m▎[22m [3mplexus/heart decompose goals → structured decisions + constraints land in the store, alongside ingested specs and your own planning turns → a later plan hits one of them → the system surfaces [1mthe conflict plus its evidence chain[22m → you pick the design[2C[1B[23m[2m▎[22m [3m→ I resolve the implementation to match.[23m[K[2C[2BThree things follow immediately.[36GFirst, th[47Ghum[51Gn [54Gs [57Ghe [61Gdjudicator, so the system's job is [3mpresentation quality[23m,[118Gno[121G automated resolution — the[149Gconflict[158Ghas[162Gto[165Garrive[172Gwith[177Gprovenance[188Gback[193Gto[196Gthe[200Gspec[205Gline[210Gor[213Gturn[218Gthat[223Gasserted[232Git,[236Gnot[240Gjust[245Gtwo[2C[1Bsentences[13Gside[18Gby[21Gside.[27GSecond,[35Gyour[40Gchoice[47Gis[50Gitself[57Ga[59Gdecision[68Gthat[73Ghas[77Gto[80Gbe[83Grecorded,[93Gwith[98Gthe[102Glosing[109Gbranch[116Gtombstoned[127Gby[130G[38;2;177;185;249msupersedes[141G[39mcarrying[150Ga[152Greason[159G—[161Gotherwise[171Gthe[175Gsame[180Gconflict[189Gresurfaces[200Gnext[205Gmonth.[212GThird,[219G"things[227GI[229Gplan[234Gout[238Gshould[245Gbe[248Gtaken[1B  into[9Gccount"[17Gsplits the cla[32Gm [35Gpace[40Galong[46Gan[49Gaxis[54Gthe[58Gcurrent[66Gmodel[72Gdoesn't[80Ghave:[86G[1mprospective[98G[22mclaims[105G(what[111Gmust[116Gor[119Gwill[124Gbe[127Gtrue[132G—[134Gplans,[141Gconstraints,[154Gdecisions)[165Gversus[172G[1mretrospective[186G[22mones[191G(what[197Gis[200Gor[203Gwas[207Gtrue[212G—[214Gthe[218G147[222Gfacts).[230GConflict[239Gdetection[249Gonly[1B  ever runs against the prospective set. That single distinction is what keeps narration out of it without needing the compiler to be clever.[K[5C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mOpen:[22m what actually counts as a conflict. This is the difference between a tool you check and a tool you mute.[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[1B← [48;2;177;185;249m[38;2;0;0;0m ☐ Conflict class [39m[49m ✔ Submit  →[K[2B[2m│[3G[22m[38;2;255;255;255m[1mWhat should the system flag as a conflict worth interrupting you for? Each class you pick is a relation to build and a false-positive source to tune — picking several means ranking and dedup become mandatory, not optional.[22m[39m[K[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;177;185;249m❯[3G[38;2;153;153;153m1.[6G[39m[[8G][10G[38;2;177;185;249mDirect contradiction[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mBoth cannot hold. "Memories key by UUID" vs "memories key by repo path." Uses `contradicts`, which exists (11 live edges). Highest precision, narrowest net — catches only conflicts stated at the same level of abstraction.[39m[K[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153m2.[39m [ ] Con[14Gtraint[21Gv[23Golation[K[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mA new plan breaks a standing rule — "never drop a fact the ontology doesn't recognise," "arteries never imports capillaries' DB layer." Needs `applies_to` (constraint→entity) and a constraint kind that is actually populated. This is the class your 1 [2C[1Blone constraint row should have been.[39m[K[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153m3.[6G[39m[[8G][10GDependency[21Gblast[27Gradius[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mYou're changing X, and 3 stored decisions depend on X. Uses `depends_on` — already in the relation vocabulary with zero live edges. Predicts conflicts before they're stated, but only as good as dependency capture.[2C[1B4.[6G[39m[[8G][10GUnresolved[21Gtension[1B [3G[38;2;153;153;153mBoth can hold, at a[23Gcost — "prefer [39Gtdlib" vs "needs sub-ms traversal." Needs a new `competes_with` relation. Most valuable for design judgment, noisiest by far, since most claim pairs are in mild tension with something.[1B[39m  [38;2;153;153;153m5. [39m[ ] [38;2;153;153;153mType[15Gsomething[39m[K[5C[1B[1mSubmit[1B[22m[38;2;153;153;153m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[1B[39m  6.[6GChat[11Gabout[17Gthis[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153mEnter to select ·[19G↑/↓ to n[28Gvigate · Esc to [45Gancel[39m[K[59;1H[45;1H[?2026l(B[?1000h[?1002h[?1003h[?1006h(B[?1000h[?1002h[?1003h[?1006h[?2026h[H[3C[40B[48;2;177;185;249m[38;2;0;0;0m☒[5C[4B[49m[38;2;78;186;101m[✔][39m[59;1H[45;1H[?2026l[?2026h[H[5C[46B[38;2;78;186;101m[✔][39m[59;1H[45;1H[?2026l[?2026h[H[44B [10GDirect contradiction[2B[38;2;177;185;249m❯[10GConstraint violation[39m[59;1H[47;1H[?2026l[?2026h[H[46B [10GConstraint violation[3B[38;2;177;185;249m❯[10GDependency blast radius[39m[59;1H[50;1H[?2026l[?2026h[H[49B [10GDependency blast radius[2B[38;2;177;185;249m❯[10GUnresolved tension[39m[59;1H[52;1H[?2026l[?2026h[H[51B [1