[39m[K[5C[1B[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39m[1mSettled:[12G[22mscope[18Gmembership[29Gstays[35Ghand-defined[48G—[50Gwhich[56Gis[59Galready[67Gexactly[75Gwhat[80G[38;2;177;185;249mart scope add[94G[39mdoes,[100Gso[103Gno[106Gmechanism[116Gchanges.[125GCardinality[137Gis[140Garbitrary:[151Gmostly[158Gsingletons,[170G[38;2;177;185;249mharness[178G[39mas[181Gthe[185Gone[189Gcluster[197G(and[202Git[205Gshould[212Gget[216G[38;2;177;185;249mheart[222G[39mand[226G[38;2;177;185;249mplexus[233G[39madded[239Gnow,[244Geven[1B [3Gunworked, so their first commit lands in the right namespac[63G rather than minting [85G scope-of-one).[K[2C[2B[1mConsequence to park:[22m with m[31Gstly-[37Gingleton[46Gscopes, a cro[60Gs-cutt[67Gng[70Gn[72Gun like [38;2;177;185;249mpgvector[89G[39mor [38;2;177;185;249mPostgres[39m beco[107Gs ~15 unrelated[123Gno[126Ges. Whether[138Gthat's a pr[150Gblem depend[162G entirely on the [180Gext an[187Gwer, so I'm[199Gnot designing around it[223Gyet.[228G[K[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m● [39mUser[8Ganswered Cl[20Gude'[26Gqu[29Gstions:[37G[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Six months from now, what is the ONE question you most want to type and get a real answer to? Ontology is driven by query — this decides which relations get built and which linkage work is worth doing. → 1 because that helps with building out [2C[1B[39m  [6G[38;2;153;153;153mprojects in noncontradictory ways (ex. building feature A at first with details 1, 2, 3 but wanting to build feature B later with details 4, 5 conflicting with 1, 2 meaning I need help resolving these issues) but I'd like all 4 eventually[2B[38;2;255;255;255m●[39m [1mSettled, and it sharpens the whole design.[46G[22mYou[50Gdon't[56Gwant[61Gdecision[70G[3mrecall[77G[23m—[79Gyou[83Gwant[88G[1mconflict detection at design time[22m:[123Gwhen[128Gyou[132Gspec[137Gfeature[145GB,[148Gthe[152Ggraph[158Gmust[163Gsurface[171Gthe[175Gprior[181Gdecisions[191Gand[195Gconstraints[207Gthat[212Gdetails[220G4[222Gand[226G5[228Gviolate.[1B[K[2C[1BThat changes what the ontology has to make work. Cosine similarity won't find these — "feature A keys memories by UUID" and "feature B keys by repo path" are semantically distant but structurally in conflict. What finds them is the [1mshared-entity arm of[2C[1B[38;2;177;185;249mexpand()[22m[39m ([38;2;177;185;249mgraph.py:110[39m), where both claims reach the same entity node. Which is precisely why grounding is load-bearing:[124Gif[127Gone[131Gclaim[137Gsays[142G[38;2;177;185;249mprimary key[154G[39mand[158Gthe[162Gother[168Gsays[173G[38;2;177;185;249mid column[39m,[184Gthey[189Ghave[194Gto[197Gcollapse[206Gto[209Gone[213Gnode[218Gor[221Gthe[225Gconflict[234Gis[237Ginvisible.[248GYour[2C[1B0/23[8Ggrounding[18Grate[23Gis[26Gthe[30Greason[37Gthis[42Gdoesn't[50Gwork[55Gtoday.[1B[K[2C[1BIt[6Galso[11Gpromotes[20G[38;2;177;185;249mconstraint[31G[39mfrom[36Ga[38Gfootnote[47Gto[50Ga[52Gfirst-class[64Gclaim[70Gkind[75G—[77Gand[81Gthere[87Gis[90Gexactly[98G[1m1 constraint[111G[22min[114Gthe[118Gdatabase,[128Gagainst[136G147[140Gfacts.[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m● [39mUser answered Claude's questions:[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Where should design constraints and decisions actually come from? Conflict detection is only as good as its input, and right now the store holds 147 facts, 8 decisions, and 1 constraint — mostly narration of work already done. → From plexus/heart [2C[1B[39m   [38;2;153;153;153mas they decompose goals, "On top of initial spec imports from plexus/heart and docs, things I plan out should also be taken into account. When conflicts arise, my goal is to be able to see them along with retrieved context for evidence, then I'll [2C[1B[39m   [38;2;153;153;153mdecide what design/feature to actually follow while you work on resolving implementation details to satisfy that"[39m[K[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39m[1mSettled — and this is the operating loop, stated cleanly:[22m[K[2C[2B[2m▎[22m [3mplexus/heart decompose goals → structured decisions + constraints land in the store, alongside ingested specs and your own planning turns → a later plan hits one of them → the system surfaces [1mthe conflict plus its evidence chain[22m → you pick the design[2C[1B[23m[2m▎[5G[22m[3m→ I resolve the implementation to match.[1B[23m[K[1B [3GThree th[12Gngs follow immediately.[36GFirst,[43Gthe[47Ghuman[53Gis[56Gthe[60Gadjudicator,[73Gso[76Gthe[80Gsystem's[89Gjob[93Gis[96G[3mpresentation quality[23m,[118Gnot[122Gautomated[132Gresolution[143G—[145Gthe[149Gconflict[158Ghas[162Gto[165Garrive[172Gwith[177Gprovenance[188Gback[193Gto[196Gthe[200Gspec[205Gline[210Gor[213Gturn[218Gthat[223Gasserted[232Git,[236Gnot[240Gjust[245Gtwo[2C[1Bsentences[13Gside[18Gby[21Gside.[27GSecond,[35Gyour[40Gchoice[47Gis[50Gitself[57Ga[59Gdecision[68Gthat[73Ghas[77Gto[80Gbe[83Grecorded,[93Gwith[98Gthe[102Glosing[109Gbranch[116Gtombstoned[127Gby[130G[38;2;177;185;249msupersedes[141G[39mcarrying[150Ga[152Greason[159G—[161Gotherwise[171Gthe[175Gsame[180Gconflict[189Gresurfaces[200Gnext[205Gmonth.[212GThird,[219G"things[227GI[229Gplan[234Gout[238Gshould[245Gbe[248Gtaken[1B  into account" splits[24Gthe[28Gclaim[34Gspace[40Galong[46Gan[49Gaxis[54Gthe[58Gcurrent[66Gmodel[72Gdoesn't[80Ghave:[86G[1mprospective[98G[22mclaims[105G(what[111Gmust[116Gor[119Gwill[124Gbe[127Gtrue[132G—[134Gplans,[141Gconstraints,[154Gdecisions)[165Gversus[172G[1mretrospective[186G[22mones[191G(what[197Gis[200Gor[203Gwas[207Gtrue[212G—[214Gthe[218G147[222Gfacts).[230GConflict[239Gdetection[249Gonly[2C[1Bever[8Gruns[13Gagainst[21Gthe[25Gprospective[37Gset.[42GThat[