des which relations get built and which linkage work is worth doing. → 1 because that helps with building out [1B[39m     [38;2;153;153;153mprojects in noncontradictory ways (ex. building feature A at first with details 1, 2, 3 but wanting to build feature B later with details 4, 5 conflicting with 1, 2 meaning I need help resolving these issues) but I'd like all 4 eventually[1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39m[1mSettled, and it sharpens the whole design.[22m You don't want decision [3mrecall[23m — you want [1mconflict detection at design time[22m: when you spec feature B, the graph must surface the prior decisions and constraints that details 4 and 5 violate.[2B [3GThat changes what the ontolog[33G has to make work. Cosine[59Gsimilarity won't find these — "featur[97G A[100Gkeys memories by UUID" and "feature B keys by repo[151Gpath" are semantically dist[179Gnt but structurally in[202Gconflict.[212GWhat finds them is the [1mshared-entity arm of[2C[1B[38;2;177;185;249mexpand()[22m[39m ([38;2;177;185;249mgraph.py:110[39m),[28Gwhere both claims reach [53Ghe same entity node. Which [81Gs precisely why grounding[107Gis[110Gload-bearing:[124Gif[127Gone[131Gclaim[137Gsays[142G[38;2;177;185;249mprimary key[154G[39mand[158Gthe[162Gother[168Gsays[173G[38;2;177;185;249mid column[39m,[184Gthey[189Ghave[194Gto[197Gcollapse[206Gto[209Gone[213Gnode[218Gor[221Gthe[225Gconflict[234Gis[237Ginvisible.[248GYour[2C[1B0/23[8Ggrounding[18Grate[23Gis[26Gthe[30Greason[37Gthis[42Gdoesn't[50Gwork[55Gtoday.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BIt[6Galso[11Gpromotes[20G[38;2;177;185;249mconstraint[31G[39mfrom[36Ga[38Gfootnote[47Gto[50Ga[52Gfirst-class[64Gclaim[70Gkind[75G—[77Gand[81Gthere[87Gis[90Gexactly[98G[1m1 constraint[111G[22min[114Gthe[118Gdatabase,[128Gagainst[136G147[140Gfacts.[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m● [39mUser answered Claude's questions:[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Wh[11Gre should design constraint[40Gand dec[48Gsio[52Gs[54Gactually come f[70Gom? Conflict detection is only as [105Good[109Gas its inp[120Gt,[123Gand right now the store[147Gholds 147 facts, 8[166Gdecisions, and[181G1 constraint — mostly narration of work already done. → From plexus/heart [5C[1Bas they decompose goals, "On top of initial spec imports from plexus/heart and docs, things I plan out should also be taken into account. When conflicts arise, my goal is to be able to see them along with retrieved context for evidence, then I'll [1B[39m [3G   [38;2;153;153;153mdecide what design/feature to actually follow while you work on resolving implementation details to satisfy that"[39m[K[2B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39m[1mSettled — and this is the operating loop, stated cleanly:[22m[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[2m▎[22m [3mplexus/heart decompose goals → structured decisions + constraints land in the store, alongside ingested specs and your own planning turns → a later plan hits one of them → the system surfaces [1mthe conflict plus its evidence chain[22m → you pick the design[2C[1B[23m[2m▎[5G[22m[3m→ I resolve the implementation to match.[2C[1B[23m[K[2C[1BThree[9Gthings[16Gfollow[23Gimmediately.[36GFirst,[43Gthe[47Ghuman[53Gis[56Gthe[60Gadjudicator,[73Gso[76Gthe[80Gsystem's[89Gjob[93Gis[96G[3mpresentation quality[23m,[118Gnot[122Gautomated[132Gresolution[143G—[145Gthe[149Gconflict[158Ghas[162Gto[165Garrive[172Gwith[177Gprovenance[188Gback[193Gto[196Gthe[200Gspec[205Gline[210Gor[213Gturn[218Gthat[223Gasserted[232Git,[236Gnot[240Gjust[245Gtwo[1B  sentences si[16Ge by side. S[29Gcond, your[40Gchoice[47Gis[50Gitself[57Ga[59Gdecision[68Gthat[73Ghas[77Gto[80Gbe[83Grecorded,[93Gwith[98Gthe[102Glosing[109Gbranch[116Gtombstoned[127Gby[130G[38;2;177;185;249msupersedes[141G[39mcarrying[150Ga[152Greason[159G—[161Gotherwise[171Gthe[175Gsame[180Gconflict[189Gresurfaces[200Gnext[205Gmonth.[212GThird,[219G"things[227GI[229Gplan[234Gout[238Gshould[245Gbe[248Gtaken[1B  into account" splits the claim space along an axis the current model doesn't have: [1mprospective[22m claims (what must or will be true — plans, constraints, decisions) versus [1mretrospective[22m ones (what is or was true — the 147 facts). Conflict detection only[K[2C[1Bever runs against the prospective set. That single distinction is what keeps narration out of it without needing the compiler to be clever.[K[5C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mOpen:[9G[22mwhat[14Gactually[23Gcounts[30Gas[33Ga[35Gconflict.[45GThis[50Gis[53Gthe[57Gdifference[68Gbetween[76Ga[78Gtool[83Gyou[87Gcheck[93Gand[97Ga[99Gtool[104Gyou[108Gmute.[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m● [39mUser[8Ganswered[17GClaude's[26Gquestions:[1B[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · What should the system flag as a conflict worth interrupting you for? Each class you pick is a relation to build and a false-positive source to tune — picking several means ranking and dedup become mandatory, not optional. → Direct contradiction, [2C[1B[39m [5G [38;2;153;153;153mConstraint violation[39m[K[2B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39m[1mSettled:[22m two[16Gtriggers only — direct contradictio[53Gand constraint violation. [38;2;177;185;249mcompetes_with[96G[39mcut from the design; [38;2;177;185;249mdepends_on[39m stays in the vocabulary but never[162Gfires an interrupt. That's [190G high-pr[199Gcision scope,[213Gand i[219G make[225G constraint capt[242Gre[246Ghe[2C[1Bcri[7Gical path,[18Gsince half y[31Gur triggers depend[50Gon a cl[58Gim k[63Gnd that curren[78Gly has one row.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mOpen:[22m the[13Ggr[16Gnularity[25Gyour constrain[40Gs[42Gattach at. Both triggers are entity-mediated, and your[97Gown constraints are phrased at wildly[135Gdiff[141Gent[145Glevels[152G—[154G[3m"arteries never imports capillaries' DB layer"[201G[23mis[204Gproject-and-subsy