ese — "feature A keys memories by UUID" and "feature B keys by repo path" are semantically distant but structurally in conflict. What finds them is the [1mshared-entity arm of[2C[1B[38;2;177;185;249mexpand()[22m[39m ([38;2;177;185;249mgraph.py:110[39m), where both claims reach the same entity node. Which is precisely why grounding is load-bearing:[124Gif[127Gone[131Gclaim[137Gsays[142G[38;2;177;185;249mprimary key[154G[39mand[158Gthe[162Gother[168Gsays[173G[38;2;177;185;249mid column[39m,[184Gthey[189Ghave[194Gto[197Gcollapse[206Gto[209Gone[213Gnode[218Gor[221Gthe[225Gconflict[234Gis[237Ginvisible.[248GYour[2C[1B0/23[8Ggrounding[18Grate[23Gis[26Gthe[30Greason[37Gthis[42Gdoesn't[50Gwork[55Gtoday.[1B[K[2C[1BIt[6Galso[11Gpromotes[20G[38;2;177;185;249mconstraint[31G[39mfrom[36Ga[38Gfootnote[47Gto[50Ga[52Gfirst-class[64Gclaim[70Gkind[75G—[77Gand[81Gthere[87Gis[90Gexactly[98G[1m1 constraint[111G[22min[114Gthe[118Gdatabase,[128Gagainst[136G147[140Gfacts.[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m● [39mUser answered Claude's questions:[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Where should design constraints and decisions actually come from? Conflict detection is only as good as its input, and right now the store holds 147 facts, 8 decisions, and 1 constraint — mostly narration of work already done. → From plexus/heart [2C[1B[39m   [38;2;153;153;153mas they decompose goals, "On top of initial spec imports from plexus/heart and docs, things I plan out should also be taken into account. When conflicts arise, my goal is to be able to see them along with retrieved context for evidence, then I'll [2C[1B[39m   [38;2;153;153;153mdecide what design/feature to actually follow while you work on resolving implementation details to satisfy that"[39m[K[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39m[1mSettled — and this is the operating loop, stated cleanly:[22m[K[2C[2B[2m▎[22m [3mplexus/heart decompose goals → structured decisions + constraints land in the store, alongside ingested specs and your own planning turns → a later plan hits one of them → the system surfaces [1mthe conflict plus its evidence chain[22m → you pick the design[2C[1B[23m[2m▎[5G[22m[3m→ I resolve the implementation to match.[1B[23m[K[1B  Three things follow immediately. First, the human is the adjudicator, so the system's job is [3mpresentation quality[23m, not automated resolution — the conflict has to arrive with provenance back to the spec line or turn that asserted it, not just two[K[2C[1Bsentences side by side.[27GSecond,[35Gyour[40Gchoice[47Gis[50Gitself[57Ga[59Gdecision[68Gthat[73Ghas[77Gto[80Gbe[83Grecorded,[93Gwith[98Gthe[102Glosing[109Gbranch[116Gtombstoned[127Gby[130G[38;2;177;185;249msupersedes[141G[39mcarrying[150Ga[152Greason[159G—[161Gotherwise[171Gthe[175Gsame[180Gconflict[189Gresurfaces[200Gnext[205Gmonth.[212GThird,[219G"things[227GI[229Gplan[234Gout[238Gshould[245Gbe[248Gtaken[2C[1Binto[8Gaccount"[17Gsplits[24Gthe[28Gclaim[34Gspace[40Galong[46Gan[49Gaxis[54Gthe[58Gcurrent[66Gmodel[72Gdoesn't[80Ghave:[86G[1mprospective[98G[22mclaims[105G(what[111Gmust[116Gor[119Gwill[124Gbe[127Gtrue[132G—[134Gplans,[141Gconstraints,[154Gdecisions)[165Gversus[172G[1mretrospective[186G[22mones[191G(what[197Gis[200Gor[203Gwas[207Gtrue[212G—[214Gthe[218G147[222Gfacts).[230GConflict[239Gdetection[249Gonly[1B [3Gever runs against the[25Gprospect[34Gv[36G set. Th[45Gt single disti[60Gc[62Gion is what keeps narration out of i[100Gwithout ne[111Gd[113Gng the compiler [130Go be clev[140Gr.[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mOpen:[9G[22mwhat[14Gactually[23Gcounts[30Gas[33Ga[35Gconflict.[45GThis[50Gis[53Gthe[57Gdifference[68Gbetween[76Ga[78Gtool[83Gyou[87Gcheck[93Gand[97Ga[99Gtool[104Gyou[108Gmute.[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m● [39mUser answered Claude's quest[32Gons:[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · What should the system flag as a conflict worth interrupting you for? Each class you pick is a relation to build and a false-positive source to tune — picking several means ranking and dedup become mandatory, not optional. → Direct contradiction, [1B[39m     [38;2;153;153;153mConstraint violation[39m[K[1B[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39m[1mSettled:[12G[22mtwo[16Gtriggers[25Gonly[30G—[32Gdirect[39Gcontradiction[53Gand[57Gconstraint[68Gviolation.[79G[38;2;177;185;249mcompetes_with[93G[39mis[96Gcut[100Gfrom[105Gthe[109Gdesign;[117G[38;2;177;185;249mdepends_on[128G[39mstays[134Gin[137Gthe[141Gvocabulary[152Gbut[156Gnever[162Gfires[168Gan[171Ginterrupt.[182GThat's[189Ga[191Ghigh-precision[206Gscope,[213Gand[217Git[220Gmakes[226Gconstraint[237Gcapture[245Gthe[1B [3Gcritical path, since half your triggers depend on a claim kind that currently has one row.[K[2B [3G[1mOpen:[22m the granularity your constraints attach[49Gat.[53GBoth[58Gtriggers[67Gare[71Gentity-mediated,[88Gand[92Gyour[97Gown[101Gconstraints[113Gare[117Gphrased[125Gat[128Gwildly[135Gdifferent[145Glevels[152G—[154G[3m"arteries never imports capillaries' DB layer"[201G[23mis[204Gproject-and-subsystem,[227G[3m"never drop a fact the [2C[1Bontology doesn't recognise"[23m is concept-level, [3m"ids are UUIDs"[23m is column-level. Pick one fixed level and half of them become unattachable. Worth noting: your extractor currently produces 23 entities across 157 claims — roughly 0.15 per claim, where[K[2C[1Bentity extraction usually yields two to five. It's under-producing[70Gbadly[76Gregardless[87Gof[90Gwhich[96Goption[103Gyou[107Gpick.[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m● [39mUser answered Claude's questions:[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · At what granularity should entities exist, so a constraint attaches where it's phrased but still matches a plan phrased differently? → Hie