Wanderin[38;2;235;159;127mg…[38;2;215;119;87m [37G[38;2;157;157;157mthinking with high effort[38;2;153;153;153m)[39m[K[59;1H[56;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[36C[51B[38;2;153;153;153mthought for 11s)[39m[K[59;1H[56;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[51B[38;2;215;119;87m*[10G[38;2;235;159;127mn[39m[59;1H[56;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[3GCentral[11Gdatabase,[21Ggroup[27Gfilters.[36GThat[41Gpart[46Gis[49Gcorrect,[58Gand[62Git's[67Gthe[71Gright[77Gcall.[2C[2B[1mWhere separation actually breaks today[22m[K[2C[2BHere's the part that matters more[37Gthan the terminology, and it's worse than the spec said.[94GIsolation is enforced [3monly by queries that remember to ask for it[23m. P[163Gstgres enforces nothing — no row-level security, no foreign key to a scop[237G. Two verified[K[2C[1Bhol[7Gs:[K[2C[2B[38;2;177;185;249m[1mgraph.stats()[39m takes [38;2;177;185;249mproject_id[39m and never uses it[22m ([38;2;177;185;249mgraph.py:180-191[39m). Both counting queries have no[102Gpredicat[111G at all. [38;2;177;185;249mart graph stats[39m already reports[152Gacross[159Gevery[165Ggroup[171Gin[174Gthe[178Gdatabase.[188GIt[191Glooks[197Gscoped,[205Gits[209Gsignature[219Gpromises[228Gscoped,[236Git[239Gisn't.[2C[2B[38;2;177;185;249m[1mart doctor --fix[39m deletes globally[22m ([38;2;177;185;249mdoctor.py:107-131[39m). [38;2;177;185;249m_collect_claims[39m, [38;2;177;185;249m_collect_entities[39m, and [38;2;177;185;249m_collect_ephemeral[39m have no p[127Goject or scope[142Gpr[145Gdicate. Run it from [38;2;177;185;249mcareer-ops[39m with [38;2;177;185;249mARTERIES_CLAIM_RETENTION_DAYS=7[39m in[216Gthat repo's env[232Gronme[238Gt, and it[248Gapplies[2C[1Bcare[9G-ops's rete[21Gtion policy [34Go [37Garness's[46Gtombstoned[57Gclaims.[65GNothing[73Gwarns[79Gyou.[2C[2BBoth are read/write paths that predate scopes and[53Gwere[58Gnever[64Grevisited.[75GAt[78Gthree[84Greal[89Gmembers[97Git's[102Ginvisible.[113GAt[116Gfifteen[124Git's[129Ga[131Gdata-loss[141Gvector.[2C[2BWorth saying what's [3mright[23m, too: [38;2;177;185;249mexpand()[39m [45Gs correct. The[60Gscope filter sits on the claim [92Gide ([38;2;177;185;249mgraph.py:167[39m) and entities[124Gcarry[130G[38;2;177;185;249mscope_id[139G[39min[142Gtheir[148Guniqueness[159Gindex,[166Gso[169Ga[171Gshared[178Gentity[185Gname[190Ggenuinely[200Gcannot[207Gleak[212Gone[216Ggroup's[224Gclaims[231Ginto[236Ganother's[2C[1Btraversal.[14GThat[19Gone[23Gwas[27Gthought[35Gthrough.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mPer-group ontologies: safe, unsafe, and the trap[22m[K[2C[2B[1mLayer 2 d[13Gvergence is[25Gthe [30Gntire point.[22m Different groups arguing about different nouns is why Layer 2 exists. No[116Gissue.[123G[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mLayer 1 divergence is a code fork.[22m [38;2;177;185;249mgraph.RELATIONS[39m, [38;2;177;185;249mgraph.ENTITY_KINDS[39m,[75Gand[79G[38;2;177;185;249mcompile._VALID_KINDS[100G[39mare[104Gsingle[111Gmodule-level[124Gtuples.[132GGive[137Gone[141Ggroup[147Gextra[153Gclaim[159Gkinds[165Gor[168Gextra[174Gedge[179Gtypes[185Gand[189G[38;2;177;185;249mcompile.py[39m,[201G[38;2;177;185;249mexpand()[39m,[211Gand[215G[38;2;177;185;249mart conflicts[229G[39mall[233Gneed[238Gper-group[2C[1Bbranching.[14GKeep[19Gthe[23Gcore[28Gidentical[38Gacross[45Gevery[51Ggroup[57Gand[61Gspend[67Gyour[72Gvariation[82Gentirely[91Gin[94GLayer[100G2.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mThe trap is "slightly different," and it has a specific mechanism.[70G[22m[38;2;177;185;249montology_terms.uri[89G[39mis[92Gthe[96G[1mprimary key[22m,[109Gglobal[116Gacross[123Gall[127Ggroups.[135G[38;2;177;185;249mload()[142G[39mruns[147G[38;2;177;185;249mDELETE ... WHERE source = %s[176G[39mthen[181G[38;2;177;185;249mINSERT ... ON CONFLICT (uri) DO UPDATE SET ..., source = EXCLUDED.source[39m.[2C[1BSo i[8G your[14Gharness vocabulary and your trading vocabulary both declare a term at the same URI,[98Gloading the second one [1mrewrites the first one's [38;2;177;185;249msource[39m column[22m. Once the scope filter [184Gxists, that term silently[210Gvanishes from the [229Gi[231Gst group's lookup[249G— no[2C[1Berror, [11Go[13Gwarning, just[29Gname that st[42Gps grounding.[56G[K[2C[2BThe[7Gsame[12Gcollision[22Ghappens[30Gone[34Glayer[40Gdown.[46G[38;2;177;185;249m_lookup()[56G[39mbuilds[63Ga[65G[38;2;177;185;249mnormalized → term[83G[39mdict[88Gwhere[94Ga[96Gkey[100Gcollision[110Gis[113Gresolved[122Gby[125G[38;2;177;185;249m_KIND_PRIORITY[39m,[141Gone[145Gwinner[152Gglobally.[162GHarness's[172G[38;2;177;185;249mModule[179G[39mand[183Gtrading's[193G[38;2;177;185;249mModule[200G[39mwould[206Gfight,[213Gand[217Gone[221Gloses[227Gsilently.[4C[2Be fix is ch[17Gap and non-[29Gegotiable: [1mnamespace every group's vocabulary under its own URI base[22m — [38;2;177;185;249mhttps://arteries.local/onto/harness#Module[39m,[144G[38;2;177;185;249m.../trading#Module[39m — and make[174G[38;2;177;185;249muri[178G[39munique[185Gper[189G[38;2;177;185;249m(source, uri)[203G[39mrather[210Gthan[215Gglobally.[225GDifferent[235Gmeanings[244Gmust[249Gbe[2C[1Bdifferent[13GURIs.[19GReusing[27Ga[29GURI[33Gis[36Ghow[40Gyou[44Gassert[51Gthat[56Gtwo[60Gthings[67Gare[71Gthe[75Gsame[80Gthing,[87Gwhich[93Gis[96Gexactly[104Gthe[108Gfalse-identity[123Gfailure[131Gthe[135Gwhole[141Gdesign[148Gis[151Gbuilt[157Gto[160Gavoid.[1B[K[2C[1B---[1B[K[2C[1BThree[9Gof[12Gthese[18Gare[22Gnew[26Gfindings[35Gnot[39Gin[42Gthe[46Gpublished[56Gspec[61G—[63Gthe[67Gunscoped[76G[38;2;177;185;249mstats()[39m,[85Gthe[89Gglobal[96G[38;2;177;185;249mdoctor --fix[39m,[110Gand[114Gthe[118GURI[122Gcollision.[133GWant[138Gme[141Gt